.TH MBUSGW-T2R 8
.SH NAME
mbusgw-t2r \- MODBUS TCP to RTU gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mbusgw-t2r
.BI /SETTINGS= file
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve MODBUS TCP clients using serial RTU devices configured in the settings file.
The DEB and RPM packages install a disabled systemd service.
Configure the serial lines and listeners before enabling it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI /SETTINGS= file
Read serial lines and listeners from
.IR file .
.TP
.BI /CONFIG= file
Read command-line options from
.IR file .
.TP
.B /CHECK
Validate the settings and exit without starting the gateway.
.TP
.BI /CONTROL= path
Set the control socket path; use NONE to disable the control channel.
The default is /var/run/mbusgw-t2r.sock.
.TP
.B /TRACE
Enable diagnostic output.
.TP
.BI /LOGFILE= file
Write messages to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI /LOGSIZE= number
Set the maximum log file size in octets.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mbusgw-t2r/modbus-t2r_settings.conf
Package settings file.
.TP
.I /var/run/mbusgw-t2r.sock
Default local control socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mbus-ctl (8),
the user guides in /usr/share/doc/mbusgw-t2r.
